 to $202 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Technology peers: P/E 15.2 vs 27.4, EV/EBITDA 10.6 vs 17.1 and P/FCF 9.4 vs 26.1 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 12% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an FCF yield of 10.6% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 8.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $137 on average, 14% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 22% clears the cost of capital of 10.0% by 12pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.37).","It runs a 50% gross margin and converts 32% of revenue into free cash flow, or 28% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.57x.","ROE of 19% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.2x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 6pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 21.7% of revenue on R&D and 4.1% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $800.9M (13% of market cap).","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 12.1, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 7.37)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 1.7% over 3 years, 7.8% over 5 years and 5.5% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 26%).","At current returns, reinvesting 41% of profits supports about 9.1% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 14.0% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 8%.","Capex runs only 0.3x depreciation (0.7% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 36, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (11 sales, net $5.0M sold).","It returns 4.7% a year to shareholders (4.7% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 2.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 1,651 employees, each generates about $1.2M of revenue, 3.3x the Technology median, and revenue has grown 10.8% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $386K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.8M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $50K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":96,"head":"Invest: trades 26% below fair value of $163; ROIC 22.4% vs WACC 10.0%.","pros":["Composite 64, above the 57 line (gates 17/26)","Trades 26% below fair value of $163","ROIC 22.4% vs WACC 10.0%","FCF margin 31.9%","Revenue grew 7.8%/yr over 5y"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":138.64,"vc":{"base":163.1,"base_src":"dcf","bear":135.56,"bull":202.13,"alt_median":112.89,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.4448,"dispersion":0.1837,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":27.4092,"ev_ebitda":17.107,"pfcf":26.1394,"pb":3.8444,"roic":0.075,"gross_margin":0.4699,"fcf_margin":0.1254,"div_yield":0.0123}},"mc_quantiles":[117.22,127.91,135.56,140.06,144.62,147.93,150.84,154.07,157.15,160.97,164.14,166.97,170.8,174.55,177.54,182.92,187.81,194.01,202.13,216.75,245.67],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.413,"discount_rate":0.473,"terminal_growth":0.027,"exit_multiple":0.087},"ticker":"CRUS","date":"2026-11-13"}